uirements."},{"industry":"energy-fossil","confidence":0.6,"rationale":"Federal research on climate, emissions, and energy impacts this sector's regulatory environment and public discourse."},{"industry":"energy-renewable","confidence":0.6,"rationale":"Federal research on energy technologies and climate directly affects this sector's market and policy landscape."},{"industry":"agriculture","confidence":0.55,"rationale":"Agricultural research conducted or funded by USDA and other agencies would be subject to these integrity standards."},{"industry":"education","confidence":0.5,"rationale":"Universities receive federal research funding and would need to comply with integrity policies in their federally supported work."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would require every federal agency that funds, conducts, or oversees scientific research to create and enforce a policy protecting scientific integrity. These policies must ensure that research conclusions are not influenced by political considerations, prohibit suppression or alteration of findings, and allow researchers to share their work. Each agency would need to appoint a Scientific Integrity Officer, establish a complaint process, provide training, and submit its policy to the White House Office of Science and Technology Policy for approval.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"Anyone who uses a phone, the internet, or a connected device.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"M001225","score":0.04131484571444916},"overlapCount":131},"meaning":{"percentile":37.62438793239615,"median":0.010636331736930488,"n":6331,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.794365105274752}},{"billId":"119-hr-7905","bioguideId":"H001090","cycle":2026,"score":0.005622437758454966,"matches":[{"industry":"health-providers","donorAmount":29800,"donorShare":0.011988519713062907,"billConfidence":0.7,"contribution":0.0050860386661479},{"industry":"pharma","donorAmount":3500,"donorShare":0.001408047617306046,"billConf