re does not pay for hearing aids. The bill also directs the Government Accountability Office to study existing programs that help people with hearing loss obtain hearing aids and related services.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People on Medicare.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"M001225","score":0.07815019980436078},"overlapCount":27},"meaning":{"percentile":22.018638445743168,"median":0.010636331736930488,"n":6331,"ordinary":[{"kind":"state-industry","text":"Health Providers is also the top donor sector for 2 other members from CA. That points to the industry being big in the state, not to anything about this member."}],"unattributedShare":0.794365105274752}},{"billId":"119-hr-4721","bioguideId":"H001090","cycle":2026,"score":0.001905628354248784,"matches":[{"industry":"agriculture","donorAmount":22500,"donorShare":0.009051734682681724,"billConfidence":0.4,"contribution":0.001905628354248784}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.794365105274752},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-4721","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"4721","title":"Healthy H2O Act","introducedDate":"2025-07-23","latestActionDate":"2025-07-23","latestActionText":"Referred to the House Committee on Agriculture.","policyArea":"Environmental Protection","subjects":[],"sponsorBioguideId":"R000603","cosponsorCount":24,"committeeNames":[],"congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/4721","industries":[{"industry":"waste-water","confidence":0.85,"rationale":"The bill directly funds water quality testing and contamination reduction, creating new revenue opportunities for water treatment and testing service providers."},{"industry":"construction","confidence":0.65,"rationale":"Grant-funded water quality improvements in rural homes and facilities would likely require installation of filtration systems and infrastructure work."},{"industry":"agriculture","confidence":0.4,"rationale":"The program is administered by USDA and targets rural areas, which may include agricultural operations, though the bill focuses on residential and childcare facilities."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would create a new grant program run by the Department of Agriculture to help people in rural areas improve their drinking water quality. Grants would go to homeowners, renters, and childcare facilities that have tested positive for health contaminants in their water, as well as to nonprofit organizations that help people test their water and reduce contamination.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People living near whatever is being regulated.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"R000603","score":0.02636879180158226},"overlapCount":25},"meaning":{"percentile":8.766387616490286,"median":0.010636331736930488,"n":6331,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.794365105274752}},{"billId":"119-hr-1657","bioguideId":"H001090","cycle":2026,"score":0.0009354670917041891,"matches":[{"industry":"pharma","donorAmount":3500,"donorShare":0.001408047617306046,"billConfidence":0.55,"contribution":0.0007464348814634462},{"industry":"retail-consumer","donorAmount":1000,"donorShare":0.0004022993192302989,"billConfidence":0.48750000000000004,"contribution":0.00018903221024074287}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"keyword-fallback","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.794365105274752},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-1657","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"1657","title":"Humane Cosmetics Act of 2025","introd